  [PASS] V1c [unique global maximum] the second variation is strictly negative, delta^2 S = -int (df)^2/f < 0, along every multiplicative mode (matches the analytic to ~1e-4), and the Lomax beats every competitor at the SAME log-moment c = 1/2 -- the exponential (S = 0.746) and t-space Gaussians of widths 0.3-1.5 (S = 0.55-0.80): 2(1+u)^{-3} IS the maximizer (strict concavity + linear constraints => unique global maximum)   S_lomax = 0.806864 > S_exp = 0.746077 > S_bump[best] = 0.803098

    1d. contrast -- the constraint CHOOSES the form:
        {1, E[u]=1} constraint:  -> exponential e^-u, S = 1 (its max-entropy value); tail slope of ln f vs ln u = -u/mu -> -12890859.6 (no power-law tail)
        {1, E[ln(1+u)]=1/2}:     -> 2(1+u)^-3, S = 3/2-ln2 = 0.806852819; tail slope = -3.000 (the power-law index -3)
        the mean constraint has NO power-law tail; the log-moment constraint
